{#
  The prices of what the providers' models consume: the page where they are
  written.

  It is a page of its own, and not a part of the one that shows the
  configuration. That one is read: it says what is running, and it is opened
  precisely when something has to be checked. This one changes something. A form
  in the middle of a reading is a click away from a write nobody meant, and the
  two are not looked at for the same reason.

  It writes **one key** of one provider object: `pricing`. Everything else is
  changed the way everything else is changed — the file, load_configuration.sh,
  a restart.

  Expected: view (src/view.js buildPricingView).
#}{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% block title %}providers' prices — webtools{% endblock %}

{% block nav %}
<nav class="index">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="elsewhere" href="/">← the configuration</a>
    {%- for entry in view.providers %}
    <a href="#provider-{{ entry.provider }}">{{ entry.provider }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</nav>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  {%- if view.failure %}
  <section class="failure">
    <h2>The configuration was not read</h2>
    <p class="detail">{{ view.failure }}</p>
    <p>Nothing below it is shown, and nothing can be written: the prices go into the documents this
      page did not manage to read.</p>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>Providers' prices</h2>
    <p class="note">One entry per provider object that <strong>names a model</strong>: those are
      the ones with something to price. What the configuration holds besides them — a provider
      object that only declares which kinds of token that provider counts, for instance — is on
      <a href="/#providers">the configuration</a>.</p>
    <p class="note">A price is the price of what a door's model consumes: <strong>one amount per
      kind of token</strong>, in hundredths of the currency's unit, per million tokens —
      <code>1500</code> is <code>15.00</code>. The kinds are the ones the provider declares in
      <code>token_kinds</code>: two kinds of token are not the same thing, and one amount for both
      would be a rate between them that nobody decided.</p>
    <p class="note">It is written into the <code>pricing</code> key of that provider object in
      Mongo, and nothing else is touched. The seed files in
      <code>webtools/configurator/configuration/</code> carry no prices: a new environment is born
      without them.</p>

    {%- if view.orphanOutcome %}
    <p class="warning">The last write was about <code>{{ view.orphanOutcome.subsystem }}</code>,
      <code>{{ view.orphanOutcome.path }}</code>, which is not among the provider objects below.
      {% if view.orphanOutcome.written %}It says it was written.{% else %}It was not written:
      <code>{{ view.orphanOutcome.reason }}</code>.{% endif %}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- for entry in view.providers %}
  <section id="provider-{{ entry.provider }}">
    <h2>{{ entry.provider }}</h2>
    {%- if entry.kinds and entry.kinds.agree %}
    <p class="note">Counts <span class="value list">{% for kind in entry.kinds.kinds %}<span class="item">{{ kind }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>
      — declared in <span class="value list">{% for where in entry.kinds.declaredIn %}<span class="item">{{ where }}</span>{% endfor %}</span></p>
    {%- elif entry.kinds %}
    <p class="warning">The kinds declared for this provider are not the same everywhere:
      <span class="value list">{% for where in entry.kinds.declaredIn %}<span class="item">{{ where }}</span>{% endfor %}</span></p>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="warning">No <code>token_kinds</code> is declared for this provider anywhere in the
      configuration.</p>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- for door in entry.doors %}
    <div class="door" id="{{ door.anchor }}">
      <p class="door-head">
        <code>{{ door.subsystem }}</code>
        <code class="path">{{ door.path }}</code>
        {%- if door.modelIsSecret %}<span class="value secret">(model: secret)</span>
        {%- else %}<span class="value string">{{ door.model }}</span>{% endif %}
      </p>

      {%- if door.outcome %}
      {%- if door.outcome.written %}
      <p class="written">Written.</p>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="warning">Not written: <code>{{ door.outcome.reason }}</code>.</p>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if door.unreadable %}
      <p class="warning">There is a <code>pricing</code> here and no amount in it can be read. What
        is stored is in the configuration, as it is stored:
        <a href="/#{{ door.subsystemAnchor }}">{{ door.subsystem }}</a>.</p>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if door.writable %}
      <form class="pricing" method="post" action="/providers/pricing">
        <input type="hidden" name="subsystem" value="{{ door.subsystem }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="provider_path" value="{{ door.path }}">
        <table class="grid">
          <thead><tr><th>kind of token</th><th>hundredths per million</th><th>stored</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for row in door.rows %}
            <tr>
              <th>{{ row.kind }}{% if not row.declared %}<span class="hint">not declared</span>{% endif %}</th>
              <td><input type="number" name="kind.{{ row.kind }}" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric"
                {%- if row.cents != null %} value="{{ row.cents }}"{% endif %}></td>
              <td>{% if row.text %}<span class="value number">{{ row.text }}{% if door.currency %} {{ door.currency }}{% endif %}</span>{% else %}<span class="absent">—</span>{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="door-foot">
          <label>currency
            <select name="currency">
              <option value=""{% if not door.currency %} selected{% endif %}>—</option>
              {%- for option in door.currencies %}
              <option value="{{ option.code }}"{% if option.selected %} selected{% endif %}>{{ option.code }}{% if not option.known %} (stored){% endif %}</option>
              {%- endfor %}
            </select>
          </label>
          <button type="submit">write the price</button>
          {%- if door.updatedAt %}<span class="updated">last written {{ door.updatedAt }}</span>
          {%- else %}<span class="absent">never written</span>{% endif %}
        </p>
        <p class="note">An amount left empty is a kind that is not priced: it is left out of what is
          written. A form with every amount empty writes nothing.</p>
      </form>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="warning">
        {%- if door.refusal == "NO_TOKEN_KINDS" %}No price can be asked for: which kinds of token
        <code>{{ entry.provider }}</code> counts is declared nowhere in the configuration.
        {%- elif door.refusal == "TOKEN_KINDS_DISAGREE" %}No price can be asked for: the kinds
        declared for <code>{{ entry.provider }}</code> differ from one declaration to another.
        {%- elif door.refusal == "PRICING_IS_SECRET" %}This price comes from
        <code>webtools/configurator/secrets/</code>, which replaces what is in Mongo at every
        <code>load_configuration.sh</code>. Written from here it would not last: change the file.
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
      {%- if door.rows.length %}
      <table class="grid">
        <thead><tr><th>kind of token</th><th>stored</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for row in door.rows %}
          <tr><th>{{ row.kind }}</th><td><span class="value number">{{ row.text }}{% if door.currency %} {{ door.currency }}{% endif %}</span></td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  {%- if not view.providers.length and not view.failure %}
  <p class="absent">No provider object names a model: there is nothing to price. What the
    configuration does hold is on <a href="/#providers">the configuration</a>.</p>
  {%- endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block footer %}
    <p>This page writes one key, <code>pricing</code>, inside a provider object. Everything else in
      the configuration is changed the way everything else is changed: edit the file in
      <code>webtools/configurator/configuration/</code>, run
      <code>webtools/configurator/load_configuration.sh</code>, restart whoever reads it. What is
      running is on <a href="/">the configuration</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
